    <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
      <body>
        <div rend="parallel">
            <p xml:id="Aink446-kilavi">pācaraikkaṇ irunta talaimakaṉ paruva varaviṉkaṇ uruvu veḷippāṭu kaṇṭu colliyatu.</p>
            <p xml:lang="en">The hero, who was in the warcamp, when the season [of his intended departure] came, saw a manifestation of the form [of his beloved] and spoke [this].</p>
              </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
          <lg xml:id="Aink446">        
        <l>mullai nāṟuṅ kūntal kamaḻkoḷa</l>
        <l>nalla kāṇkuva māa yōyē</l>
        <l>pācaṟai yaruntoḻi lutavinaṅ</l>
        <l>kātaṉaṉ ṉāṭṭup pōtarum poḻutē.</l>
        </lg>  
 <lg xml:lang="en">                    
<l>[Your] tresses, fragrant with jasmine, taking on [an even sweeter] scent,<note xml:lang="en" place="foot">I understand the idea to be that once the hero returns, the heroine's pleasant qualities, such as her jasmine-scented hair will be elevated, and the couple will enjoy good times. Accordingly, I understand the phrase <foreign xml:lang="ta-Latn">nalla kāṇkuvam</foreign> as an idiomatic way to that he sees good times in their future.</note></l>
<l>we shall see good things, O dark one,</l>
<l>when, having helped with the difficult task in the warcamp,</l>
<l>[I] return to our beloved fine land.</l>
</lg>                      
        </div>
      </body>
    </text>
